CuV probe: an iron block with a water channel, 14 MeV point source
c Synthetic test problem for the cell-under-voxel readers: an iron block
c (x, y -60..60, z 0..30) bored by a water cylinder (r 15) along z, in a
c void sphere (r 120) under a point source. The box meshes reach past the
c sphere, so their corner voxels hold the graveyard too. Regenerate with
c D1SUNED 4.1.3.2: d1suned4132 i=input tasks 8
1  1 -7.87  -1 2        imp:n=1 $ iron block
2  2 -1.0   -2          imp:n=1 $ water channel
3  0        -3 1        imp:n=1 $ void around
99 0         3          imp:n=0 $ graveyard

1 RPP -60 60 -60 60 0 30
2 RCC 0 0 0  0 0 30  15
3 SO 120

MODE N
M1 26056.31c 1
M2 1001.31c 2 8016.31c 1
SDEF PAR=N POS=0 0 -20 ERG=14
NPS 2e4
PRDMP j j 1
c The cylinder goes first, with 20 energy bins (see README).
FMESH4:N GEOM=CYL AXS 0 0 1 VEC 1 0 0 ORIGIN 0 0 0
         IMESH 15 40 80 IINTS 1 1 1
         JMESH 30 60 JINTS 1 1
         KMESH 1 KINTS 1
         EMESH 1e-8 3e-8 1e-7 3e-7 1e-6 3e-6 1e-5 3e-5 1e-4 3e-4
               1e-3 3e-3 1e-2 3e-2 0.1 0.3 1 3 7.0711 14.5
         OUT=CUV
         SPPTS=1000 SPMODE=RAND
FC14 CuV rectangular, 4 energy bins
FMESH14:N GEOM=XYZ ORIGIN -100 -100 0
         IMESH 100 IINTS 2
         JMESH 100 JINTS 2
         KMESH 20 60 KINTS 1 1
         EMESH 1e-6 0.1 1 14.5
         OUT=CUV
         SPPTS=1000 SPMODE=RAND
FC24 Twin of 14 without CuV
FMESH24:N GEOM=XYZ ORIGIN -100 -100 0
         IMESH 100 IINTS 2
         JMESH 100 JINTS 2
         KMESH 20 60 KINTS 1 1
         EMESH 1e-6 0.1 1 14.5
FMESH44:N GEOM=XYZ ORIGIN -50 -50 0 TR=1
         IMESH 50 IINTS 2
         JMESH 50 JINTS 1
         KMESH 40 KINTS 2
         OUT=CUV
         SPPTS=500 SPMODE=RAND
TR1 0 0 -10  0.8 0.6 0  -0.6 0.8 0  0 0 1
